id: pm-brief-vj2y
title: "pm brief diverge: pre-merge multi-agent item collision preview"
description: "Adds 'pm brief diverge' subcommand that previews pm item divergence between two git branches BEFORE merging. Shows which items both branches touched and whether the field-aware merge driver will resolve them cleanly (union-safe) or produce a real conflict (field-collision, duplicate-id, delete-vs-edit). Includes a fence check for .gitattributes/git-config merge driver installation. Supports markdown/text/json/slack formats with deterministic ordering and token budgeting."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-ux,merge-safety,multi-agent
created_at: "2026-07-24T21:10:37.746Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T22:13:36.481Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-24T22:13:36.481Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "pm brief diverge previews divergence between base/head git refs: classifies each touched pm item as head-only, base-only, union-safe, field-collision, duplicate-id, or delete-vs-edit; checks merge driver fence (.gitattributes + git config); supports --base/--head/--include-clean/--max-items/--token-budget/--format/--output; deterministic ordering (duplicate-id > delete-vs-edit > field-collision > union-safe > one-sided), tie-break by id; markdown/text/json/slack renderers; pure functions exported and unit-tested; one end-to-end integration test with real git repo; npm run typecheck/build/test pass."
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:19:30.710Z",pi-agent,"Implemented pm brief diverge: git readers (resolveRepoRoot, resolveRef, detectDefaultBase, mergeBase, listChangedPaths, readBlob), path model (pmRootRelFromCtx), event identity (parseHistoryJsonl, eventKey, newEvents, countMalformedLines), field extraction (changedFieldPaths, normalizeFieldPath, BENIGN_FIELDS), per-item classification (classifyItemDivergence: 6 kinds — head-only, base-only, unchanged, duplicate-id, delete-vs-edit, field-collision, union-safe), fence check (evaluateFence), aggregate (buildDivergence: verdict precedence, deterministic ordering, token budget), 4 renderers (markdown/text/json/slack), command registration with all flags. 27 unit tests + 1 end-to-end integration test (real git repo + real pm CLI). Gates: typecheck OK, build OK, 86/86 tests pass, changelog:check OK. Production proof: ran all 4 formats against a real divergent git repo — verdict review-required, item1 field-collision on /metadata/status, item2 union-safe (priority vs assignee), item3 base-only. Co-Authored-By: pi-agent <noreply@anthropic.com>"
  "2026-07-24T21:27:52.796Z",claude,"Independent verification (claude, 2026-07-24): gates green in worktree — typecheck rc=0, build OK, 88/88 tests pass (86 from pi + 2 added for the fixes below).\n\nREAL-DATA GROUND-TRUTH PROOF: built a scratch git repo (3 items, field-aware fence installed via pm merge install), branched agent-a (I1 status=in_progress, I2 priority=3) and agent-b from the same ancestor (I1 status=blocked, I2 assignee=bob, I3 title). 'pm brief diverge --base agent-b' predicted: I1 field-collision on /metadata/status, I2 union-safe (assignee vs priority), I3 base-only, verdict review-required, fence ok. Then ran the actual 'git merge agent-b': it CONFLICTED on exactly .agents/pm/tasks/<I1>.toon and auto-merged <I2>.toon cleanly — prediction matched ground truth item-for-item. All four formats (markdown/json/text/slack) render.\n\nEDGE CASES verified live: clean verdict when only head advances; --include-clean lists the one-sided item; fence-missing reports both missing pieces (.gitattributes entries + merge.*.driver config) and puts 'pm merge install' first; duplicate-id detected as high severity with 'pm history <id> --verify' recommended; unknown ref exits 2 with a clear message.\n\nTWO DEFECTS FOUND AND FIXED during verification:\n1. Unrelated histories were only disclosed in markdown prose. JSON.stringify drops the undefined ancestorSha, so a JSON consumer saw verdict=clean with no way to know there was no merge base. Added an explicit always-present unrelatedHistories boolean + JSON round-trip test.\n2. The recommended command was a bare 'git merge <base>' even with no merge base, which git refuses outright ('refusing to merge unrelated histories'). Now emits 'git merge --allow-unrelated-histories <base>' in that case only.\nAlso documented the command in README (it was entirely undocumented)."
  "2026-07-24T21:52:57.584Z",claude,"Review round 2 (CodeRabbit, 4 findings, all accepted and fixed):\n1. MAJOR — listChangedPaths/readBlob collapsed every non-zero git exit into empty/absent, so a spawn failure, killed process or 64 MiB maxBuffer overflow rendered as a clean verdict. This was the single most dangerous defect in the feature: for a pre-merge safety check, silence read as safety. Added assertGitRan (spawn error + signal) and per-caller status handling; readBlob now matches git's absent-path stderr explicitly so a corrupt object cannot masquerade as a missing item; mergeBase treats ONLY exit 1 as unrelated-histories.\n2. MINOR — pmRootRelFromCtx rejected any rel starting with '..', including a legitimate in-repo directory like ..cache/pm; and an empty rel (pm root == repo root) produced prefixes like /history/ that match nothing, silently reporting no divergence. Now tests the parent-directory boundary and fails loudly on the repo-root case.\n3. MAJOR — parseHistoryJsonl and countMalformedLines disagreed: an object line without ts was dropped from events but not counted as malformed, under-reporting exactly the data loss this command exists to surface; and every ledger was JSON-parsed twice. Consolidated into single-pass scanHistoryJsonl returning {events, malformedLines}; the two old exports are now thin wrappers so they can never diverge again.\n4. MINOR — this record carried no tests[] evidence for its acceptance criteria. Added.\n\nGates after fixes: typecheck rc=0, build OK, 93/93 tests pass (5 new covering each finding). Live end-to-end re-verified: same scratch two-branch repo still predicts field-collision on /metadata/status and union-safe for the disjoint-field item, with the real git merge conflicting on exactly the predicted file."
  "2026-07-24T22:13:26.581Z",claude,"Review round 3 (CodeRabbit, 6 remaining findings) + a process defect found while auditing.\n\nPROCESS DEFECT (most important): the round-2 replies on PR #37 told CodeRabbit the fixes shipped in commit 1694709. They did not. checkAttrMerge, the summarizeSide signature cleanup and the binary-search token trim existed ONLY in the local worktree and were never committed or pushed, so the branch under review never contained them. Every round-2 claim has now been re-verified against the pushed tree and the record corrected on the PR.\n\nFINDINGS RESOLVED THIS ROUND:\n1. MAJOR (perf/correctness) — the diverge command re-listed the ENTIRE pm tree once per item per side: 'git ls-tree -r <sha> -- <pmRoot>' ran 3N times for N changed items, then string-scanned each result. The tree depends only on the revision, so it is now listed once per SHA into a Set of item ids (3 scans total, independent of N). The old closure also swallowed a non-zero ls-tree exit as 'item absent', which would misclassify items as delete-vs-edit on a git failure; it now goes through the hardened listChangedPaths, which raises instead.\n2. MINOR (test integrity) — the integration test printed 'skipping' and returned when pm was absent, so a missing pm CLI reported as a PASSING no-assertion test. Now calls t.skip('pm not on PATH'), and uses os.tmpdir() instead of a hardcoded /tmp.\n3. TRIVIAL-but-material (test integrity) — the 'end-to-end' test re-implemented the command's own gathering pipeline (its own readBlobAt/toonPresent/id-collection/buildDivergence wiring), so the shipped command path was never executed: ref resolution, pmRootRelFromCtx, listChangedPaths, classifyPaths, the check-attr fence probe, renderer selection and --output were all untested, and the duplicated helpers could drift from the real ones without any test failing. The test now activates the extension, resolves the registered 'brief diverge' command and runs it against the fixture repo for both --format json --output and the default markdown render, asserting on what the command actually produced. Proven non-vacuous by mutation: breaking pmRootRel wiring in index.ts now fails this test (95/96), where the old duplicated-pipeline version stayed green.\n4/5/6. Unused summarizeSide parameter, git check-attr as the authoritative fence resolver, and the O(n^2) token-trim loop were already fixed in the worktree; they are only now actually committed.\n\nGROUND TRUTH RE-VERIFIED against a real merge after the hoist: scratch repo, 5 items, fence installed, agent-a (I1 status, I2 priority) vs agent-b (I1 status, I2 assignee, I3 title) from a common ancestor. 'pm brief diverge --base agent-b' predicted field-collision on /metadata/status for I1, union-safe for I2, base-only for I3, verdict review-required. The real 'git merge agent-b' from a clean tree then conflicted on exactly .agents/pm/tasks/<I1>.toon and auto-merged <I2>.toon retaining BOTH sides (priority=1 from agent-a AND assignee=bob from agent-b). Prediction matched ground truth item-for-item.\n\nGates after fixes: typecheck rc=0, build OK, 96/96 tests pass."
tests[4]{command,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  "node --test dist-test/brief.test.js --test-name-pattern \"brief diverge / buildDivergence\"",project,300
  "node --test dist-test/brief.test.js --test-name-pattern \"brief diverge / review round 2 hardening\"",project,300
  "node --test dist-test/brief.test.js --test-name-pattern \"brief diverge end-to-end\"",project,300
  npm test,project,300
close_reason: "Shipped in PR #37: pm brief diverge predicts pre-merge pm item collisions between two branches; verified against a real git merge item-for-item after three review rounds."
